;; Exact example from docs/reference/language/continuations.md: a continuation
;; captured at top level, saved, and re-invoked until a counter runs out.
;;
;; This is a REGRESSION TEST for ledger SW-52. The bytecode VM used to print
;; "1" and then an unbounded stream of "2", never terminating: a continuation
;; snapshotted and restored the whole operand stack, and because the VM binds
;; every top-level define to an operand-stack slot, re-entry rolled `n` back to
;; its capture-time value along with the control state. The loop guard could
;; therefore never advance. R7RS call/cc captures the control state, not the
;; store, so `set!` must survive re-entry.
;;
;; EXPECTED on native JIT, native AOT and the bytecode VM: 1 / 2 / 3 / done.
(define k #f)
(define n 0)
(display (+ 1 (call/cc (lambda (c) (set! k c) 0))))
(newline)
(set! n (+ n 1))
(if (< n 3) (k n))
(display "done") (newline)
